            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="PLU02" sex="2">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Annabella</forename>
                        <surname>Plumptre</surname>
                        <addName>Bell</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1769">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1838-12-18"/>
                    <occupation>writer</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>See the entry on her Annabella Plumptre's sister <persName key="PLU01">Anne Plumptre</persName>
    and Anne's <title>DNB</title> entry, which discusses both sisters. See also the entry on their brother James Plumptre.
    Godwin distinguishes between A and B/Bell Plumptre, the former for her sister Anne and the later for Annabella. Entries for Miss Plumptre have been 
    coded for the older sister as it would be conventional to refer to her as Miss Plumptre.<lb/>
  
 Godwin sees Anne mainly in Norwich, save for a visit in early 1802, when she may be starting on her European tour.  
</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
